{"version":1,"summary":"A SIGTERM, SIGINT or SIGHUP now stops the launcher's brain and removes its run directory.",
"files":[{"path":"agent/internal/cli/cli.go","summary":"Turns the three signals into a context for Run.","annotations":[{"newRange":[44,49],"summary":"Main converts SIGTERM, SIGINT and SIGHUP into Options.Interrupt and restores default handling after the first signal.","rationale":"Go ends the process on SIGTERM without running defers, so the run directory stayed. Now Run returns normally and its deferred RemoveAll runs. A second signal still kills the launcher at once. Verified by TestSignalLeavesNoRunDirectory and the verify-verilex recipe.","author":"fm/verilex-agent-sigterm"}]},
{"path":"agent/internal/run/run.go","summary":"Ends the brain phase on the interrupt and returns inconclusive.","annotations":[{"newRange":[261,264],"summary":"Run returns inconclusive right after an interrupted brain, before verdict.Decide.","rationale":"A partial run must not print a verdict, because a red from half the checks would be final. Exit stays 2, so exit-code behavior is unchanged.","author":"fm/verilex-agent-sigterm"}]}]}
